\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot 36} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-31671/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/8e599d9e02d6e6926083818414fd3d5b6f7cf853286e2ec019cdd0bf16d35dff"]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/4417e908d15e6a350d27386726eda84b8ed4775387ec33b0b0913c99ab88fa5b" :answer/id #uuid "a9345321-da07-5850-a176-a2be4eeb0fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/d446fc145ed745083ee9c1e72e471380a749fdc0c518f06b05d1f856478ac04f" :answer/id #uuid "3f596ada-4e46-59bc-8450-fc4adac082c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/75f24d724a2a6d414f728df584af3b618487aa0d483abda8872d7ed031138d94" :answer/id #uuid "7a09b8da-215e-5c71-bc12-cec348a35046" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/d99e47350762385b2972f8918c0dd8c9d2684502d59789da9cea764af55bbeeb" :answer/id #uuid "20993aad-d1f0-546a-a266-393eb4483c51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/b56e8fd4c1673f3a5e0a7ecbf4d0ce3a35fb506359c0b4147e585a2936f394b1" :answer/id #uuid "4cfdcdc4-0a76-596d-8c20-d93e101fd58d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca1caf9e-e19b-5eea-ae2c-7ade6678c5da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/d99e47350762385b2972f8918c0dd8c9d2684502d59789da9cea764af55bbeeb" :answer-field/choices ["q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/4417e908d15e6a350d27386726eda84b8ed4775387ec33b0b0913c99ab88fa5b" "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/d446fc145ed745083ee9c1e72e471380a749fdc0c518f06b05d1f856478ac04f" "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/75f24d724a2a6d414f728df584af3b618487aa0d483abda8872d7ed031138d94" "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/d99e47350762385b2972f8918c0dd8c9d2684502d59789da9cea764af55bbeeb" "q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13/b56e8fd4c1673f3a5e0a7ecbf4d0ce3a35fb506359c0b4147e585a2936f394b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186344831 :question/answer-fields 17592186344832] {:db/id 17592186344831 :db/ensure [:question/validate] :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+2,\\,12t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨2(0)+2,12(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(0)|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|⟨2,0⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-31674/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/fe70a6e5ab2b8dda4e53e56da2190113285bf4b4cc879f1a5f92948a16b50c13"]} {:db/id 17592186088078 :db/ensure [:question/validate] :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{t}^{1/2}+8t,\\,3{t}^{2}-8t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{1/2}+8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-8t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{-1/2}+8,\\,6t-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨3(1)^{-1/2}+8,\\,6(1)-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+8,\\,6-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨11,\\,-2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186344860 :db/ensure [:question/validate] :question/problem "The position vector $r,$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+3,\\,{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+1⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the acceleration is\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨15{t}^{2}-4t,\\,4{t}^{3}-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-6t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30t-4,\\,12{t}^{2}-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨30(2)-4,\\,12(2)^{2}-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨60-4,\\,48-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨56,\\,42⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(2)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(2)| & =|⟨56,\\,42⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{56}^{2}+{42}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3136+1764} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4900} \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the acceleration at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is $70\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}.$"} {:db/id "q-82337/selection/mathematical-correction-units-v1/c1f97ed90f99d323d0e024ddd1af58673b0d077d16b8e57ce3fff3b093aeb1f5/f583d44249377d444a2366a2ac28ea4ca0711b051a9d7762185c3fd2cab933c6" :answer/id #uuid "260b7bcd-cac8-5cad-917c-f